@startuml
title RustServer.Auth — authentication and portal routing

hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 80

actor Browser
participant "LoginPageController\n/login" as LoginPage
participant "Static assets\n/login.css, /login.js" as Assets
participant "ASP.NET Core antiforgery\n/api/auth/csrf" as Antiforgery
participant "LoginController\n/api/auth/login" as Login
participant "Google login controller\n/api/auth/google/login" as GoogleLogin
participant "Google middleware\n/signin-google" as GoogleMiddleware
participant "Steam login controller\n/api/auth/steam/login" as SteamLogin
participant "Steam middleware\n/signin-steam" as SteamMiddleware
participant "ASP.NET Core Identity" as Identity
participant "PortalRedirectController\n/portal" as Portal
participant "AdminPortalController\n/admin" as AdminPortal
participant "Other applications\n/player, /dashboard" as Applications
database "Identity data store" as Store

note right of Identity
  RustServer.Auth owns /login, authentication APIs,
  /portal and /admin. The platform owns /player and
  /dashboard; Auth does not implement either route.
end note

== Display the login page ==

Browser -> LoginPage: GET /login
LoginPage --> Browser: 200 OK — wwwroot/index.html (text/html)
Browser -> Assets: GET /login.css and GET /login.js
Assets --> Browser: 200 OK
Browser -> Antiforgery: GET /api/auth/csrf
Antiforgery --> Browser: 200 OK — { token }

== Username and password ==

Browser -> Login: POST /api/auth/login\ncredentials + X-CSRF-TOKEN
Login -> Identity: PasswordSignInAsync()
Identity -> Store: Validate credentials and lockout state
alt Credentials accepted
  Store --> Identity: User and role claims
  Identity --> Browser: 200 OK + RustServer.Auth cookie
  Browser -> Portal: GET /portal
else Credentials rejected or CSRF validation fails
  Login --> Browser: 401 Unauthorized or 400 Bad Request
  Browser -> LoginPage: Remain on /login and display error
end

== Google sign-in ==

Browser -> GoogleLogin: GET /api/auth/google/login
GoogleLogin -> GoogleMiddleware: Challenge with application callback\n/api/auth/google/login-callback
GoogleMiddleware --> Browser: 302 Google authorization endpoint
Browser -> GoogleMiddleware: GET /signin-google after Google authorization
GoogleMiddleware --> Browser: 302 application callback
Browser -> GoogleLogin: GET /api/auth/google/login-callback
GoogleLogin -> Identity: GetExternalLoginInfoAsync()\nand ExternalLoginSignInAsync()
alt Linked Google account signs in
  GoogleLogin --> Browser: 302 Location: /portal
else Account is not linked or callback data is invalid
  GoogleLogin --> Browser: 302 Location: /login?googleError=1
end

== Steam sign-in ==

Browser -> SteamLogin: GET /api/auth/steam/login
SteamLogin -> SteamMiddleware: Challenge with application callback\n/api/auth/steam/login-callback
SteamMiddleware --> Browser: 302 Steam OpenID endpoint
Browser -> SteamMiddleware: GET /signin-steam after Steam verification
SteamMiddleware --> Browser: 302 application callback
Browser -> SteamLogin: GET /api/auth/steam/login-callback
SteamLogin -> Identity: Get or create Steam user
alt Steam sign-in succeeds
  SteamLogin --> Browser: 302 Location: /portal
else Callback data is invalid or sign-in fails
  SteamLogin --> Browser: 302 Location: /login?steamError=1
end

== Route an authenticated user ==

Browser -> Portal: GET /portal
alt No authenticated user
  Portal --> Browser: 302 Location: /login
else Administrator
  Portal --> Browser: 302 Location: /admin
  Browser -> AdminPortal: GET /admin
  AdminPortal -> Identity: Validate current user and Admin role
  Identity --> AdminPortal: Access decision
  AdminPortal --> Browser: 200 OK or 404 Not Found
else Player
  Portal --> Browser: 302 Location: /player
  Browser -> Applications: GET /player
end

@enduml
